:[46,131],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Forecast methods":[132,200],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Forecast methods#{1}":[134,200],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Default forecast period lengths":[201,226],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Default forecast period lengths#{1}":[203,204],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Default forecast period lengths#Default period lengths common to all data sources":[205,220],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Default forecast period lengths#Default period lengths common to all data sources#{1}":[207,220],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Default forecast period lengths#Default period lengths unique to MetricBase":[221,226],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Default forecast period lengths#Default period lengths unique to MetricBase#{1}":[223,226],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Related":[227,230],"#Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization#Related#{1}":[229,230]},"outlinks":[{"title":"time series visualization","target":"create-dv-time-series-ac","line":22},{"title":"Forecast methods","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/now-intelligence/configure-forecast-ts-viz.md","line":60},{"title":"Automatic selection of forecast methods","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/now-intelligence/configure-forecast-ts-viz.md","line":60},{"title":"Default forecast period lengths","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/now-intelligence/configure-forecast-ts-viz.md","line":68},{"title":"Create time series data visualizations","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/now-intelligence/create-dv-time-series-ac.md","line":125},{"title":"Performance Analytics scores forecasts","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/now-intelligence/performance-analytics/c_ForecastingData.md","line":130},{"title":"Medium article","target":"https://williamkoehrsen.medium.com/random-forest-simple-explanation-377895a60d2d","line":182},{"title":"Create time series data visualizations","target":"create-dv-time-series-ac","line":229}],"metadata":{"title":"Configure a forecast in a time series data visualization","description":"If a time series visualization is configured to show forecasts, you can configure the forecasts for that visualization.Forecasting uses standard statistical methods. You can select a method or let the system choose one automatically.If you are a statistics expert, you can select a forecast method manually. By default, the instance chooses the best method for you automatically, based on the fit of the method.Forecast periods have a default length that depends on the frequency of the data sources. Not all data sources have the same frequencies.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/now-intelligence/configure-forecast-ts-viz.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"task","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":5,"breadcrumb":["Time series visualizations","Create","Data visualizations","Platform Analytics experience","Platform Analytics"],"tags":["#now-intelligence","#type-task"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/now-intelligence/configure-forecast-ts-viz.md"},
